[1m[38;5;231mThe logger keeps `username` in logs as-is. Is that right?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mLog it plainly (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mBest debugging signal — you can trace one user's failing session. It is PII sitting in logs, so retention becomes a
[39m     [38;5;246mpolicy question later.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Hash it
     [38;5;246mCorrelate a user's events across lines without storing the identity. You cannot tell who it was without the [39m
     [38;5;246moriginal value.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Add username to the denylist
     [38;5;246mMaximum privacy. Login logs become nearly useless for tracing an individual report.[39m
